---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="terms-hero">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">Last updated: September 2025</p>
    </section>

    <section class="terms-content">
      <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing and using Code Like It's 198x ("the website"), you accept and agree to be bound
        by the terms and provision of this agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Educational Use</h2>
      <p>
        This website provides educational content about retro computing and assembly programming.
        All content is provided for learning purposes and should be used responsibly.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Open Source License</h2>
      <p>
        All code examples and educational content are provided under the MIT License unless
        otherwise specified. You are free to use, modify, and distribute the code in accordance with
        the license terms.
      </p>

      <h2>4. User Conduct</h2>
      <p>When using our website and community resources, you agree to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the content for lawful purposes only</li>
        <li>Respect intellectual property rights</li>
        <li>Not distribute malicious code or harmful content</li>
        <li>Be respectful in community interactions</li>
        <li>Follow the community guidelines when participating in discussions</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The educational content on this website is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind,
        express or implied. We make no guarantees about the accuracy, completeness, or suitability
        of the information provided.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        In no event shall Code Like It's 198x, its contributors, or affiliates be liable for any
        damages arising from the use or inability to use the content on this website.
      </p>

      <h2>7. External Links</h2>
      <p>
        This website may contain links to external websites. We are not responsible for the content
        or privacy practices of these external sites.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Contributions</h2>
      <p>
        If you contribute code, documentation, or other content to the project, you agree to license
        your contributions under the same open source license as the project.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Modifications to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to modify these terms at any time. Changes will be effective
        immediately upon posting to the website.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Contact Information</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these Terms of Service, please open an issue on our
        <a href="https://github.com/code198x/code198x/issues" target="_blank">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  .terms-hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: 3rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .terms-hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .last-updated {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .terms-content {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .terms-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .terms-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .terms-content ul {
    margin-left: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .terms-content li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .terms-content a {
    color: var(--link-color, #667eea);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .terms-content a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
